0e6a8ec103793e7a96cd46294efebb5f70cd6064fd01cdaa8268","event_uuid":"0d8ba0e7-9921-408d-9f70-baac9a7f2a79","position":{"commit_sha":"dd9e886a0ae46e4c5e4d2fa7f6dc322c3d67f1b6","position":"1785783746979409001-0d8ba0e7-9921-408d-9f70-baac9a7f2a79"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Census drift after origin/main refresh (50 commits landed since this plan was written): the detector now finds 16 sites, not 15. NEW sites (landed with the J11/5200 live-DC work): tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_mutations.py:107 and :1020 (RUN:30721408463), tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_inbound_assignee_oracle_discriminates_5200.py:133 (RUN:30763838558). Some original sites may have shifted line numbers or been removed. IMPLEMENTATION NOTE: treat the description's 15-site list as the adjudicated-replacement guide, but RE-RUN the detector against the implementation worktree's HEAD for the authoritative remediation list — new sites get the same treatment (move narrative to a ticket, cite the ticket). This drift while the ticket sat unclaimed is itself evidence for the CI-guard half of the plan: rot accrues actively, roughly 1 new violating site per ~17 commits in this window.","timestamp":1785706605023419001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed as Gerrit change 1309's parent — change 1304 (commit f2b2d0b410, 'Add comment-hygiene gate; fix rot-prone refs'), MERGED with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1. Delivered: scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py (block-level comment+docstring scan; SHA-like hex, run/job/thread ids, date+incident-verb triggers; ticket-id/alias acceptor; context: external escape hatch; EXCLUDED_FILES self-exclusion), CI wiring in _build-and-test.yml, remediation of every detector hit at HEAD (census drifted from the 17 as-of-plan pins; the detector re-run at HEAD was authoritative), policy note in CONTRIBUTING.md, and tests/unit/test_comment_hygiene_guard.py covering the FP gotchas ('bug surfaced', 'ticket dirs' not accepted; 4x4 ids + word-triple aliases accepted; escape hatch honored). Tree scans clean with zero in-tree suppressions. AC boxes flipped post-merge per close protocol.","timestamp":1785782998561517001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Close attempt REJECTED by the completion verifier — a correct catch, recorded here as gate evidence: tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_differ_field_contract.py:12 still carried raw SHA 183fd51ac2. Root cause was an acceptor FALSE-ACCEPT in the delivered guard: the word-triple-alias pattern matched the hyphen-joined file name 'sync-hardening-proposal.md', so the block scanned green and the remediation sweep skipped it. Also found: tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_dc_epic_link_parent_39c1.py:15 (run-id 30784592232) merged 42 minutes before the guard landed — a race the tree-clean test now fails on main. Fix pushed as Gerrit change 1310: alias pattern rejects path/extension context (sentence-final aliases still accept), both sites remediated per the plan's adjudicated forms, two new gotcha tests pin the false-accept and the sentence-final accept. Will re-close after 1310 merges.","timestamp":1785783746979409001}],"created_at":1785640248467756001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"7e90aac5-fdc7-4b9c-b8d5-d8bd6b229ce6","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ba72-7bad-0c88-4fc8"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nSource comments carry commit SHAs, run/thread IDs, and dated incident narratives that rot: 8 of 18 cited SHAs in the tree are ALREADY unresolvable (Gerrit rebase-on-submit guarantees pre-land SHA death), and run IDs die with retention windows. Policy: source is for current state + concise rationale; the ticket system owns historical detail. The detector is NET-NEW code (the prototype that produced the corpus numbers ran in the planning session and was not committed; its measured results — 0 FPs, 15 violating sites, 47 compliant blocks on the then-current tree — are recorded here as design evidence, and the corpus is re-derived by running the new detector at the implementation worktree's HEAD, which is authoritative; the ticket comment records census drift to 16 sites already).\n\n## Approach\n(1) Remediate every detector hit at HEAD (17 pinned above as-of-plan: the original 15 census sites, of which 2 were later found under src/ in the PR-375 bucket, plus 3 post-plan RUN-id sites minus overlap) — each maps to a specific replacement already adjudicated: delete.py:188 drop dead-SHA mechanism sentence; classify.py:310 + test_frozen_census.py:79 cite epic 3006-e198; reconcile.py:588 + tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_commit_binding_store_failure.py:10 (module docstring's 'cf93b2b7ad failure class') describe the failure class in behavioral terms (story findable via git log -S); test_ci_actionlint_install.py cite bug 4e99-b2ae; test_plan_review_explain.py:308 (docstring narrates 'the class of bug `62933ff62` fixed for plan-review deep-links' — a raw dead SHA) drop the SHA and cite bug c7e3-dd16; test_execution_mode_dispatch.py cite 454a-9266; test_inbound_differ_field_contract.py point at the live CONTRACT block + story a130-2b7c; 7 PR-#375 sites keep 'PR #375 review' and drop raw thread ids (tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_inbound_leaf_bodies.py:63/69/210/310/451 + src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/typed_dispatch.py:128 + src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound.py:233); test_at_most_one_invariant.py:199 drop e04e0b289c; 3 RUN-id sites from the post-plan J11/5200 work (tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_mutations.py:163/1638-context + tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_inbound_assignee_oracle_discriminates_5200.py:20-context, runs 30721408463/30763838558) get the same treatment — narrative to a ticket, cite the ticket. Line numbers are as-of-plan pins; the re-run detector census at HEAD is the authoritative remediation list and may add/retire sites (same adjudicated replacement rules apply). (2) CI guard (detector is NET-NEW per Context; prior art/reuse: it follows the repo's scripts/check_*.py guard convention — check()/main() shape, wired as a named step in .github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml like check_verify_gate_parity.py — landing as scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py): block-level scan (comment blocks + AST docstrings); rot-prone = SHA-like hex >=7 with digits+letters (denylist ed25519/sha256 etc), run/job/thread id >=8 digits after keyword, date+evidence-verb — defined as: a date token (YYYY-MM-DD or 'Month DD, YYYY') in the same block as a past-tense incident verb from the ENUMERATED set {failed, broke, regressed, fixed, caught, observed, hit, crashed, flaked} (the block narrates a dated incident); 'surfaced' is deliberately EXCLUDED from the verb set — the prototype's 'bug surfaced' FP introduces current-state explanation, not an incident date, and must not trigger. Acceptor interaction: triggers are evaluated first, then a triggered block is ACCEPTED iff it cites a qualifying id — the gotcha cases must not trigger at all (they never reach the acceptor); ACCEPTED when the block cites a ticket/epic/story/bug/rec/ADR id — hex-grouped (4x4 like 3006-e198-…) or word-triple alias (three lowercase hyphen-joined dictionary words, e.g. robe-creek-zealot, the store's human alias form) — pointing history at the ticket system is the sanctioned pattern; escape hatch 'context: external' for vendor-pinned refs (changelogs, upstream issue SHAs). Self-exclusion (sibling-guard convention): the detector's own unit-test module (tests/unit/test_comment_hygiene_guard.py, whose fixtures MUST contain live rot-prone tokens as RED/gotcha cases) is excluded from the tree scan by an EXCLUDED_FILES tuple in the script — the same mechanism check_criteria_vocabulary.py uses (scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py:38); fixtures live only in that one excluded module, so 'zero suppressions' means zero IN-TREE escape-hatch uses, with the single structural exclusion visible at the top of the script.\n\n## Scope\n- the detector-hit sites listed above (src/ + tests/; authoritative list = detector re-run at HEAD)\n- scripts/ or CI lint module implementing the detector + workflow wiring\n- short policy note in CONTRIBUTING.md or docs (source=current state, tickets=history)\n\n## Testing\nDetector unit tests re-derived at HEAD (prototype-measured shape: ~15-17 pre-fix sites RED, ~47 compliant blocks green — exact counts pinned when the detector lands), the acceptor-arm gotchas ('bug surfaced', 'ticket dirs' must NOT accept; grouped 4x4 ids and word-triple aliases MUST accept), escape hatch honored. Post-remediation tree scans clean.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] All detector-hit sites at HEAD remediated, each in one of three sanctioned forms: (a) cites a ticket/epic/story/bug id that RESOLVES in the ticket system (spot-check via rebar show), (b) drops the rot-prone token leaving durable current-state prose (PR-#375 bucket keeps 'PR #375 review', drops raw thread ids), or (c) replaces a SHA narrative with a behavioral description findable via git log -S (the test_commit_binding_store_failure.py form).\n- [x] CI guard fails on reintroduced rot-prone refs, passes the current remediated tree with zero suppressions.\n- [x] Escape hatch documented; policy note landed.\n- [x] Detector unit tests cover the FP gotchas measured in the planning prototype ('bug surfaced'/'ticket dirs' NOT accepted; grouped 4x4 ids and word-triple aliases accepted; escape hatch honored).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/","reason":"comment-hygiene detector"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/delete.py","reason":"remediate site"},{"path":"tests/","reason":"remediate 10+ test sites"},{"path":".github/workflows/test.yml","reason":"CI guard wiring"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97"],["relates_to","ba72-7bad-0c88-4fc8"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97","parent_status_uuid":"ec9072cd-a807-401a-8a02-d78a467fcd3a","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["hygiene","ci"],"ticket_id":"b047-267f-3c3d-4374","ticket_type":"story","title":"Comment hygiene: remediate rot-prone historical refs in code + CI guard","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d96973bc-b466-4ae7-b4a1-f8f02227cefb","0d05935f-257b-4ff6-b587-a3aa743946bc","01e7fbc1-1e12-4b69-89f5-3354438bb26b","e03c5297-9226-4999-b777-d45024cc0fa7","2ce20a26-18ea-40f5-a32d-6af7a0223fa0","5253670d-db15-44ee-86c8-496fd469f501","da3b0d3b-26a3-4536-9539-ffa84f9ab154","ec9072cd-a807-401a-8a02-d78a467fcd3a","91dacd8a-d712-4ddd-bfb3-234db13b2c44","7e90aac5-fdc7-4b9c-b8d5-d8bd6b229ce6","b0bfd8ca-b110-41b5-b9e1-5dca6b96de31","b8d2bb8f-e580-45d0-882b-6f0e20a69784","0d8ba0e7-9921-408d-9f70-baac9a7f2a79"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785783746979409002,"uuid":"eed761e2-05bd-4f74-a72b-3b9f90aa6a80"}